# Console widget-pointer test — the pointer's gesture vocabulary on a real
# console: a click focuses the widget under it, a click on an accordion header
# (its [-]/[+] glyph included) folds it, and a click on terminal with no widget
# under it drops the focus AND hands the mouse back to the terminal.
#
#   bin/metatron-console --from classes --steps bin/test/console-widget-mouse.steps
#
# The widget is created @<notes> — i.e. STORE-BACKED, exactly like the live
# think_widget — because that is the case that used to fold in the space while
# still drawing itself unfolded (an AccordionWidget read its construction-time
# snapshot instead of the space; see AccordionWidget.field).
#
# It is TOP_LEFT anchored, so its box starts at row 2, column 1:
#   ┌ notes [-] ┐
#   1         13
# the header is that whole first row.  A click is an SGR press AND release —
# the release (lowercase "m") is what resets jline's button state, or every
# later press reads as a drag.  "\x3b" is how a ";" is written in a steps file,
# since ";" separates steps.  (The harness lowercases the transcript for its
# case-insensitive matching, which is why needles here are lowercase.)

WAIT_CONSOLE

# --- create a store-backed accordion and float it ---
MARK float
SEND accordion_widget::[title=>'notes',body=>"one\ntwo\nthree",style=>[anchor=>top_left,width=>40,height=>10]]@<notes>
SLEEP 1
SEND @<notes>.display()
WAIT │ one 20
SILENT float ▶ 2

# --- click the widget: it takes the focus (and the mouse with it) ---
MARK click
RAW b"\x1b[<0\x3b5\x3b4M"
RAW b"\x1b[<0\x3b5\x3b4m"
SLEEP 1
WAIT_SINCE click ▶ 10

# --- click its header: that focuses, it does NOT fold (a folded accordion
# --- draws only its header, which reads as "my text disappeared")
MARK header
RAW b"\x1b[<0\x3b4\x3b2M"
RAW b"\x1b[<0\x3b4\x3b2m"
SLEEP 1
SILENT header notes [+] 2
# (a header click on an already-focused widget changes nothing, so nudge a
# redraw to prove the text is still drawn)
KEY alt+w
WAIT_SINCE header │ one 5

# --- click the header: the accordion folds ---
MARK collapse
RAW b"\x1b[<0\x3b10\x3b2M"
RAW b"\x1b[<0\x3b10\x3b2m"
SLEEP 1
WAIT_SINCE collapse notes [+] 10
SILENT collapse │ one 3

# --- a folded header says how much it is holding, so "folded" can never be
# --- mistaken for "the text never arrived" (notes holds three body lines) ---
WAIT_SINCE collapse notes [+] 3 5

# --- and the fold is in the SPACE, so an update does not undo it ---
MARK update
SEND @<notes>>>=[body=>+*"four\n"].display()
SLEEP 2
SILENT update notes [-] 3

# --- click it again: the accordion unfolds ---
MARK expand
RAW b"\x1b[<0\x3b10\x3b2M"
RAW b"\x1b[<0\x3b10\x3b2m"
SLEEP 1
WAIT_SINCE expand │ one 10

# --- click terminal with no widget under it: unfocus + hand the mouse back ---
MARK blur
RAW b"\x1b[<0\x3b70\x3b30M"
RAW b"\x1b[<0\x3b70\x3b30m"
SLEEP 1
SLEEP 1
SILENT blur ▶ 3
SEND :widgets
SLEEP 1
WAIT_SINCE blur 1 floating widget
SILENT blur [active] 3

# --- the pointer is the terminal's now, so the keyboard re-arms it ---
MARK rearm
KEY alt+w
WAIT_SINCE rearm ▶ 10
MARK click2
RAW b"\x1b[<0\x3b10\x3b2M"
RAW b"\x1b[<0\x3b10\x3b2m"
SLEEP 1
WAIT_SINCE click2 notes [+] 10
